power: supply: max77705_charger: bound the AICL loop, skip it in OTG mode

max77705_aicl_irq() steps CHGIN_LIM down, 100 ms at a time, until
CHG_INT_OK reports AICL_OK. Two ways it never ends:

- With the OTG boost running, CHGIN sees the boost's own VBUS as valid
  input and AICL never settles. On the Galaxy Tab S8+ this held the
  MAX77705 interrupt thread (shared by the charger, gauge and Type-C
  children) in the loop indefinitely: the input limit walked down from
  1775 mA to 925 mA while the CCIC's detach interrupt sat undelivered,
  the Type-C driver never saw the detach and VBUS stayed on.
- Nothing stops the decrement at the field's minimum; regval-- from 0
  wraps and the field write masks it to 3.2 A.

Return at once while the boost and OTG bits are set, and stop at code
3, the 100 mA floor.

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c
index 5d7e7e3d5..8c6615e95 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c
@@ -44,9 +44,18 @@ static enum power_supply_property max77705_charger_props[] = {
 static irqreturn_t max77705_aicl_irq(int irq, void *irq_drv_data)
 {
 	struct max77705_charger_data *chg = irq_drv_data;
-	unsigned int regval, irq_status;
+	unsigned int regval, irq_status, mode;
 	int err;
 
+	/*
+	 * With the OTG boost running, CHGIN sees the boost's own VBUS and
+	 * AICL never settles; stepping the limit down would never end and
+	 * would hold the shared MFD interrupt thread.
+	 */
+	err = regmap_field_read(chg->rfield[MAX77705_MODE], &mode);
+	if (err < 0 || (mode & MAX77705_OTG_CTRL) == MAX77705_OTG_CTRL)
+		return IRQ_HANDLED;
+
 	err = regmap_read(chg->regmap, MAX77705_CHG_REG_INT_OK, &irq_status);
 	if (err < 0)
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
@@ -58,6 +67,10 @@ static irqreturn_t max77705_aicl_irq(int irq, void *irq_drv_data)
 		if (err < 0)
 			return IRQ_HANDLED;
 
+		/* codes 0-3 are all the 100 mA minimum; stop there */
+		if (regval <= 3)
+			return IRQ_HANDLED;
+
 		regval--;
 
 		err = regmap_field_write(chg->rfield[MAX77705_CHG_CHGIN_LIM], regval);
